<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mashhad</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mashhad is a city in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorasan">Khorasan</a>, and an important Shia pilgrimage centre around the shrine of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">Imam</a> Reza. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a> made it a principal seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a>. After Nader's assassination in 1747, his grandson Shahrukh held a reduced Afsharid realm centred on Mashhad.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mashhad.jpg" alt="Mashhad" width="320" height="194" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ALI0513 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_View_of_Koohsangi_street,_Mashhad,_Iran.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
